  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "r2-f6-resolved",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "pre-existing",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:120",
      "summary": "Round-2 blocking f6-exact-words-shell-operator is resolved in e1ced9f: a gate with shell syntax only counts in the shell form with the exact (trimmed) line; split words are refused (round-2 probe E1 now gate-receipt-not-gate; test [review-7-r2-1]). Round-1 f1 stays resolved (5d, 5e refused). Round-2 f7 is narrowed: relative ./sh and tools/bash are refused (A4, A5; test [review-7-r2-2]). Round-2 f8 (pwsh -command case, cmd -c) is unchanged and not repeated."
    },
    {
      "id": "f9-plain-gate-newline",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:125",
      "summary": "For a plain gate, the shell-form line is compared after splitting on any whitespace, so a newline between words passes; a shell runs each line as a separate command. Probe P1: gate \"node gate.mjs true\" (gate red), genuine receipt of sh -c \"node gate.mjs\\ntrue\" is green and pushes. Realistic gates end in a non-command word and stay red (P2 \"... test\" is red). Simple fix: for a plain gate also require the line to hold no shell syntax (shellSyntax includes \\n), or split only on spaces and tabs.",
      "assumption": "Needs a newline deliberately written into the -c argument and a gate whose last word is a passing command; no ordinary mistake produces it, so it is the deliberate-fake class, not a spec-7-1 failure."
    },
    {
      "id": "f10-absolute-or-path-fake-shell",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:113",
      "summary": "The f7 fix rejects only relative program paths. Still accepted: an absolute path to a committed no-op project script named bash (C5), a POSIX relative path that looks like a Windows drive path, C:/x/bash, because win32.isAbsolute is true (C4), and a symlink named bash on PATH or elsewhere pointing to echo/true (S1, S3). All need a deliberate fake; refusing absolute paths inside the project root and win32 paths on POSIX would close C4 and C5. State it with the forged-footer limit.",
      "assumption": "Same class as the stated forged-footer limit and the round-2 f7 follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "cmd.exe and powershell are not on this Mac: Windows paths were checked with hand-written footers only.",
